  message: "DONE in PR #1225 (merged a53ff18377). READING (b): it was a defect, two of them, both in the data-flow extractor, plus a third in the verdict envelope. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/simiv_fix_09262026/RESULT.md.\n\nHOW IT WAS TOLD APART. The production verify-claims run was instrumented by wrapping _ddg_taint_reaches with its escape_sites out-param:\n  p_pt_enc (with open(..) as f: f.write(e)): barrier=[4] -> None, NO escapes, forfeit_refutation=True; uncovered_semantic_lines -> {5}. The with clause is recorded as the synthetic CFG statement context_manager_enter, which no AST node carries, so populate_def_use_for_cfg never extracted it (f undefined) and the coverage gate counted the clause as uncovered code -> the whole function forfeits -> the barrier walk can never return False.\n  p_nowith (open(\"o\",\"wb\").write(e)): unguarded walk escaped (no_heir). The statement's uses were overwritten by the INNER open(...) call: same (line, col, \"call\") key, pre-order walk, uses [e] -> [].\nFIXES: outermost node wins in populate_def_use_for_cfg; CfgStatement.ast_node_type + one statement_match_key for both passes; a python with_clause handler (defines the as-targets, uses the values) so a covered clause is a modelled one.\nTHIRD DEFECT, found because the fix \"didn't work\": _require_coverage_to_confirm rebuilt verdicts field by field and dropped sanitized_flows (+5 fields) on the withheld branch, so details said \"1 flow(s) ... pass through a sanitizer\" beside \"sanitized_flows\": 0. Now dataclasses.replace.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, the item's own three fixtures re-run on the merged CLI (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gotun_recheck_09252026/{p_pt_enc,p_nowith,p_min}, claims_pt.yaml):\n  p_pt_enc  inconclusive  sanitized_flows 1  evidence_count 0   (was violated, sanitized 0)\n  p_nowith  inconclusive  sanitized_flows 1  evidence_count 0   (was violated, sanitized 0)\n  p_min     inconclusive  sanitized_flows 1  evidence_count 0   (was inconclusive, sanitized 0 -- probably credited all along and hidden by the dropped field)\ninconclusive is the coverage gate (cryptography.fernet has no I/O catalogue rows), a separate question. Control on the production path: plaintext written beside the encrypted value stays violated (packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_py_with_clause_and_sanitizer_credit.py, red before the fix).\n\nCOHORT A/B, 5 python repos: no verdict / evidence / sanitized / caveat-kind / flows_removed_by_walk change; walk 'unconfirmed' stays 0; functions_forfeited 115->10, 12->5, 238->84, 566->360, 1968->1487. check-self-claims: 18 unchanged.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that the credit fires for every shape or language. Only python has a with-clause handler (only python declares context_manager); the outermost-wins fix is core and applies to every extractor."  # 4f95
